{"id": "byd-2026-05-20-013", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["byd"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["ev_sales", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["[否定]record", "[否定]slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "IEA: Global EV sales headed for another record year despite the slowdown", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/04/BYD-Denza-Z9-GT-EV-price.jpeg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1400\" /></div><p>According to the International Energy Agency’s (IEA) new Global EV Outlook, electric car sales are expected to hit 23 million in 2026, making up nearly 30% of all new cars sold worldwide. That comes after EV sales topped 20 million in 2025, up 20% year over year, with 1 in 4 new cars sold globally now electric.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-la", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/05/19/iea-global-ev-sales-headed-for-another-record-year-despite-the-slowdown/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-20-014", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Mercedes unveils AMG GT EV: 1,153hp, 0-60 in 2s, 11min charge, fake V8 noise", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/05/26C0129_003.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1500\" /></div><p>We’re in LA for the world premiere of Mercedes’ upcoming ultra-high performance EV, the AMG GT 4-Door Coupe, with race-ready features and more power than any Mercedes ever released… along with silly fake V8 noises (but at least you can turn them off).</p>\n\n\n\n<p>(<em>Update: We got a test ride! Scroll to the bottom of the post)</em></p>\n\n\n\n <a ", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/05/19/mercedes-unveils-amg-gt-ev-1153hp-0-60-in-2s-11min-charge-fake-v8-noise/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-20-015", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "American energy sector to invest $100B in battery storage by 2030 [update]", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2025/05/wartsila_energy_252e4e.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p>Last year, the smart money had the American energy sector investing a cool $100 billion (with a “b”) in battery storage for sustainable energy. Today, those batteries aren’t just supporting wind and solar, they’re propping up AI data centers – and the investments are just getting bigger.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-la", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/05/19/american-energy-sector-set-to-invest-100b-in-battery-storage-by-2030/", "type": "rss"}]}
